From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:13:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: find MLD stations by link address in the TX status
 callbacks

A non-AP MLD is registered under its MLD MAC address, but Authentication
and Association responses are addressed to the link address the peer used.
The lookup in the TX status callbacks therefore misses, so the association
is never completed and the peer waits for an EAPOL frame that is never
sent. Fall back to the link address lookup.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -8335,6 +8335,10 @@ static void handle_auth_cb(struct hostap
 	bool success_status;
 
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (!sta) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "handle_auth_cb: STA " MACSTR
 			   " not found",
@@ -8515,6 +8519,12 @@ static void handle_assoc_cb(struct hosta
 	int new_assoc = 1;
 
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* A non-AP MLD is registered under its MLD MAC address, while the
+	 * response was addressed to the link address it associated from. */
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (!sta) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "handle_assoc_cb: STA " MACSTR " not found",
 			   MAC2STR(mgmt->da));
